WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:15.015
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

00:18.393 --> 00:19.644
Are you telling me

00:20.770 --> 00:22.439
to fabricate the truth?

00:22.522 --> 00:23.356
What, fabricate?

00:23.940 --> 00:25.066
Well, aren't you?

00:25.567 --> 00:28.611
I never followed them to the hospital
or saw anything.

00:29.112 --> 00:31.614
How could I have seen Mr. Kim
hurting Min-hui--

00:31.698 --> 00:33.033
You punk!

00:35.201 --> 00:37.704
You listen to me carefully.

00:38.580 --> 00:41.332
This isn't fabrication.

00:41.416 --> 00:44.711
This is the truth.
An undeniable truth based on all we know.

00:44.794 --> 00:46.880
Why else would Kim Su-hun
show up at the park

00:46.963 --> 00:49.382
after seeing the letter
about the CCTV footage?

00:49.883 --> 00:53.428
That was him effectively admitting
to the crime through his actions!

00:58.099 --> 01:00.643
Lee Kang. Are you still listening?

01:04.147 --> 01:06.483
Even so, I can't
write about something I didn't see.

01:06.983 --> 01:08.151
That would be lying.

01:09.110 --> 01:11.321
What did you tell me time and time again?

01:11.821 --> 01:14.657
That a writer must be objective
and see reality as it is.

01:14.741 --> 01:15.658
Be truthful.

01:15.742 --> 01:16.659
That's right!

01:17.160 --> 01:18.787
I know. I do.

01:19.370 --> 01:21.956
I'm not saying we should commit fraud.

01:22.540 --> 01:26.669
We're just filling in a small gap
in the truth with our imagination.

01:26.753 --> 01:28.797
That's what stories are all about.

01:28.880 --> 01:30.507
Fiction that strives for the truth.

01:30.590 --> 01:33.635
That's the true power of stories!

01:36.554 --> 01:37.847
I don't know.

01:39.349 --> 01:41.518
What do you intend
by writing a story like that?

01:41.601 --> 01:46.356
We need to expose that bastard
Kim Su-hun's true colors to the world.

01:47.941 --> 01:50.193
That's the duty of a writer
who knows the truth.

01:52.195 --> 01:53.071
No.

01:54.739 --> 01:55.949
I can't do it.

01:56.449 --> 01:59.786
Besides, I can't write anymore.
My dad's not doing well.

02:02.872 --> 02:05.583
To be honest, I had a really tough week.

02:06.501 --> 02:08.294
If you want it written, do it yourself.

02:09.671 --> 02:11.506
What? Me?

02:12.340 --> 02:13.299
How could I?

02:13.800 --> 02:15.426
You're the writer, kid!

02:15.510 --> 02:18.638
Why not? You used to write before.

02:20.140 --> 02:23.852
You're the writer of this story now,
so do whatever you want with it.

02:25.812 --> 02:26.896
I'm sorry, Mr. Heo.

02:26.980 --> 02:28.314
Hey, Lee Kang!

02:28.398 --> 02:30.233
I'm not done talking, hey!

02:30.316 --> 02:31.901
You bastard, don't hang up!

02:32.694 --> 02:35.113
You ungrateful bastard!

03:05.393 --> 03:06.352
What did he say?

03:11.441 --> 03:13.151
I'm the writer now?

03:43.223 --> 03:44.432
I'm…

03:45.725 --> 03:47.393
I'm the writer now?

04:00.573 --> 04:01.741
I'm the writer now?

04:07.455 --> 04:11.209
I couldn't really tell
what the author was trying to say.

04:12.418 --> 04:14.087
It made me think,

04:14.587 --> 04:17.090
why bother writing
when you have nothing to say?

04:19.175 --> 04:21.177
It's okay to live as is.

04:22.720 --> 04:24.973
But, above all else,

04:25.974 --> 04:28.017
you should relearn sentence structures.

04:40.196 --> 04:43.116
Watch closely, Kim Su-hun,
you son of a bitch.

04:45.159 --> 04:47.203
I'll show you.

06:03.071 --> 06:06.449
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW
BY HEO MUN-OH

06:47.240 --> 06:48.074
Yes.

06:49.909 --> 06:51.577
It wasn't all a dream.

06:57.333 --> 07:00.002
This is my novel.

07:01.462 --> 07:02.547
This is mine.

07:09.554 --> 07:11.139
My second novel.

07:44.464 --> 07:45.840
Well, look who it is.

07:46.549 --> 07:49.051
-Well, if it isn't Mr. Newbie Writer.
-Mr. Heo?

07:49.135 --> 07:51.929
-Calling me early today--
-Why weren't you answering?

07:53.306 --> 07:55.766
You crazy bastard,
yelling at me like some…

07:55.850 --> 07:57.185
You rude little shit!

07:57.268 --> 07:58.936
I've been calling you all night!

07:59.645 --> 08:00.563
What?

08:03.065 --> 08:04.901
LEE KANG
13 MISSED CALLS

08:07.778 --> 08:09.864
Why? What is it?

08:11.657 --> 08:12.617
Mr. Heo.

08:13.201 --> 08:16.370
Brace yourself
for what I'm about to tell you.

08:17.163 --> 08:19.415
You know the last scene you told me about?

08:20.082 --> 08:21.792
The final scene at the hospital.

08:21.876 --> 08:24.879
There's an even darker ending,
and I think it just unfolded!

08:26.422 --> 08:29.217
What do you mean by a darker ending?

09:01.499 --> 09:05.044
I woke up in the middle of the night
to find I had missed calls.

09:05.127 --> 09:06.254
SE-YUN
2 MISSED CALLS

09:09.799 --> 09:11.968
I had a bad feeling, so I called back.

09:12.051 --> 09:15.888
The person you are calling
is not available…

09:26.732 --> 09:28.442
Kang! Lee Kang!

09:29.485 --> 09:31.445
Kang… Kang!

09:32.363 --> 09:33.489
Lee Kang.

09:36.325 --> 09:37.410
Kang.

09:38.619 --> 09:40.746
Kang, are you listening?

09:45.376 --> 09:47.712
Dad is trying to kill Mom and me.

09:51.424 --> 09:53.593
He's going to burn the place down.

09:55.261 --> 09:56.721
He's going to kill her?

09:57.305 --> 09:58.222
Eun-joo?

09:59.682 --> 10:01.309
And burn the place down?

10:01.392 --> 10:02.768
The end of the message

10:03.436 --> 10:05.313
was truly horrifying.

10:58.199 --> 10:59.909
That was the last thing I heard.

11:04.288 --> 11:06.540
I'm so scared, Mr. Heo.

11:07.875 --> 11:09.085
What do we do now?

11:12.630 --> 11:15.383
That son of a bitch has finally lost it.

11:15.883 --> 11:17.551
He's trying to bury any evidence.

11:19.845 --> 11:23.057
He's found out
that Eun-joo knows everything.

11:23.140 --> 11:24.433
Please, Mr. Heo.

11:24.934 --> 11:28.938
I'm headed to Seoul right now,
but it'll take a while to get there, so

11:29.438 --> 11:31.273
could you head there now?

11:32.108 --> 11:33.359
-Find out what's--
-Address.

11:33.442 --> 11:35.695
Just give me the address.

11:38.614 --> 11:39.990
Kim Su-hun, you bastard.

11:41.158 --> 11:43.244
Just how far are you planning to go?

11:45.371 --> 11:47.581
How far are you planning to go, damn it?

13:13.167 --> 13:14.084
Yun…

13:17.254 --> 13:18.672
Where's Yun?

13:29.266 --> 13:30.226
Tell me.

13:33.270 --> 13:34.188
Tell me

13:35.064 --> 13:37.817
that our Yun is okay.

13:42.363 --> 13:43.489
Don't tell me…

13:44.740 --> 13:46.033
Please tell me you didn't.

13:47.993 --> 13:49.203
You didn't, did you?

13:51.080 --> 13:52.164
Tell me now.

13:52.706 --> 13:53.874
Tell me now!

13:56.126 --> 13:57.211
After all this,

13:58.170 --> 14:00.381
can you still call yourself a father?

14:01.590 --> 14:03.926
How could you?

14:04.009 --> 14:05.469
Goddammit!

14:07.513 --> 14:08.889
Why'd you go and do that?

14:09.682 --> 14:11.976
Why did you have to go digging around?

14:14.353 --> 14:15.896
You were better off not knowing.

14:39.753 --> 14:41.088
If you had just ignored it…

14:41.964 --> 14:43.090
That way…

14:49.263 --> 14:52.391
we could have kept pretending to be happy!

15:08.240 --> 15:11.035
No, you son of a bitch!

15:12.286 --> 15:14.538
Kim Su-hun, you son of a bitch! No!

15:16.749 --> 15:19.585
This ending is unacceptable.

15:21.837 --> 15:23.839
Not for my Eun-joo.

15:24.924 --> 15:26.550
Not my dear Eun-joo.

15:27.551 --> 15:29.470
You bastard, I'll kill you.

15:36.060 --> 15:36.894
EMERGENCY SERVICES

15:53.577 --> 15:54.453
What the heck?

15:55.412 --> 15:56.455
Hey, get in.

16:06.340 --> 16:09.218
License plate 6904, you're speeding.
Pull over to the right.

16:11.929 --> 16:14.765
6904, pull over to the right, now!

16:16.934 --> 16:19.311
Good. This is actually for the best!

16:19.895 --> 16:21.563
Stay right behind me, okay?

16:21.647 --> 16:23.565
Follow and keep up!

16:23.649 --> 16:25.859
This is how the world
will find out about you!

16:26.527 --> 16:29.154
You're finished.
You're fucked, you bastard!

16:30.114 --> 16:32.157
License plate 6904, pull over!

16:36.036 --> 16:37.913
Is he crazy? On his tail.

16:37.997 --> 16:39.623
You got it, sir.

16:57.433 --> 16:58.559
Get out of the way.

17:08.986 --> 17:10.487
Move!

17:11.864 --> 17:12.781
Move!

17:17.953 --> 17:18.787
Should we leave?

17:18.871 --> 17:21.540
-Let's wait and see.
-All these bloody prank calls.

17:21.623 --> 17:24.001
-When did they call?
-What are you doing?

17:24.084 --> 17:26.336
Why are you still standing out here?

17:26.420 --> 17:28.839
Right, are you the one
who reported the fire?

17:28.922 --> 17:29.923
Yes, that's me.

17:30.424 --> 17:34.219
What are you waiting for?
You need to get in there now!

17:34.303 --> 17:38.932
That bastard is in there right now,
setting the damn place on fire!

17:39.767 --> 17:41.810
Hey! Kim Su-hun!

17:41.894 --> 17:43.312
Hey, you bastard!

17:43.395 --> 17:44.688
Open the door right now!

17:44.772 --> 17:46.315
Open the door! Open it!

17:46.398 --> 17:49.693
What fire are you talking about, sir?

17:49.777 --> 17:52.488
What's all this? An emergency patient?
What's going on here?

17:53.072 --> 17:56.241
Well, we're wondering the same thing.

17:58.118 --> 18:00.537
Sir, perhaps you made a mistake?

18:00.621 --> 18:01.914
A mistake?

18:02.414 --> 18:05.209
Do you people have any idea
what's going on in there?

18:05.292 --> 18:08.587
What's going on here?
Thank you for all your hard work.

18:08.670 --> 18:10.506
-Open up now, you bastard!
-Sir.

18:10.589 --> 18:14.301
Do you know how many red lights you ran?
Why didn't you stop?

18:14.384 --> 18:15.969
Good, you're here.

18:16.053 --> 18:17.763
Cops. You're the police.

18:17.846 --> 18:19.723
Hurry up and get this door open!

18:19.807 --> 18:21.892
That's not important right now!

18:21.975 --> 18:23.102
No, she's not dead yet.

18:23.185 --> 18:25.479
I have to save Eun-joo.
We have to save her!

18:25.562 --> 18:26.939
Eun-joo can't die!

18:27.731 --> 18:30.484
Come on, get this damn door open now!

18:30.984 --> 18:34.738
Do you all know the writer Kim Su-hun?
Well? Kim Su-hun, the writer?

18:34.822 --> 18:37.741
That shameless bastard
who won't stop showing up on TV.

18:37.825 --> 18:41.620
That bastard is in there right now
killing people. You hear me?

18:41.703 --> 18:44.748
People are dying in there,
you motherfuckers!

18:44.832 --> 18:47.126
Open up now! Hurry up and open the door!

18:47.209 --> 18:49.503
-Please calm down.
-Kim Su-hun, you son of a bitch!

18:49.586 --> 18:51.922
-Sir.
-We get it, so please just calm down.

18:52.005 --> 18:53.715
-Sir, please.
-Let go! It's all true!

18:53.799 --> 18:55.926
Professor? Professor Heo Mun-oh!

19:02.057 --> 19:03.892
What are you doing at my house, sir?

19:06.770 --> 19:07.604
Hey, Heo Mun-oh.

19:11.441 --> 19:12.276
Mun-oh?

19:18.574 --> 19:20.284
You're Mun-oh, right?

19:24.746 --> 19:26.748
What's all this about?

19:35.507 --> 19:36.633
Mun-oh?

19:39.011 --> 19:40.554
What's this about?

19:45.976 --> 19:47.144
Mun-oh?

19:48.187 --> 19:49.021
What's wrong?

20:04.620 --> 20:08.290
I don't know what's going on,
but why don't we step inside and…

21:21.822 --> 21:23.156
LEE KANG

21:24.408 --> 21:25.534
Answer the phone.

21:26.952 --> 21:28.704
Just pick up, you bastard.

21:30.205 --> 21:31.415
Come on, pick up.

21:31.999 --> 21:33.709
Pick up, you bastard!

21:34.710 --> 21:35.961
Answer already!

21:38.005 --> 21:40.048
Pick up the damn phone!

21:40.590 --> 21:42.718
-Son of a bitch.
-The person you are calling…

21:53.061 --> 21:55.564
MR. HEO MUN-OH

22:05.907 --> 22:06.992
Hey, Lee Kang!

22:08.952 --> 22:09.911
Stop right there!

22:12.664 --> 22:13.498
Hey!

22:14.249 --> 22:15.709
What the heck is wrong with you?

22:16.293 --> 22:18.128
Stop right there. We need to talk.

22:18.628 --> 22:21.465
What happened? Hey, stop right there!

22:21.965 --> 22:22.966
You little shit.

22:33.685 --> 22:34.561
Stop right there!

23:17.062 --> 23:18.605
Where did that bastard go?

23:55.600 --> 23:56.435
Honey.

23:57.644 --> 23:58.478
Why the suitcase?

24:11.241 --> 24:13.702
Was that bastard Lee Kang here?

24:20.250 --> 24:22.002
So he came by here,

24:23.420 --> 24:24.254
right?

24:25.964 --> 24:27.007
That bastard was here?

24:28.258 --> 24:29.217
What did he say?

24:29.926 --> 24:31.219
What did you two talk about?

24:34.764 --> 24:36.016
Answer me, damn it!

24:36.850 --> 24:40.061
What did that bastard tell you?

24:40.562 --> 24:43.482
That bastard is a complete nutjob!

24:54.451 --> 24:56.870
Now that I think about it,
it's a little strange.

24:58.038 --> 24:59.289
Why would he come here

25:00.248 --> 25:01.708
when I wasn't even home?

25:05.045 --> 25:05.921
You're smirking?

25:08.048 --> 25:09.716
What's with that smirk?

25:10.884 --> 25:12.219
Did you two do something?

25:14.387 --> 25:18.058
Did you get drunk and fool around
with that young bastard in broad daylight?

25:38.703 --> 25:40.038
No way.

25:42.207 --> 25:44.000
You wouldn't.

25:45.919 --> 25:48.171
He's not a kid. He's an adult.

25:51.049 --> 25:52.008
So what?

26:16.866 --> 26:18.952
How could he when he has a wife like you?

26:22.205 --> 26:24.624
Mr. Heo sure is a fool, isn't he?

27:03.038 --> 27:04.748
Sure, feel free to imagine

27:05.415 --> 27:06.916
what we did.

27:07.876 --> 27:09.336
That's your specialty, isn't it?

27:12.422 --> 27:13.548
"We"?

27:16.009 --> 27:17.719
Have you actually lost it?

27:19.471 --> 27:21.931
-Why, so suddenly…
-It wasn't sudden.

27:23.516 --> 27:25.268
Kang came to see me

27:26.019 --> 27:28.855
while you were obsessing
over the story about Ahn Eun-joo.

27:52.545 --> 27:53.463
I see.

27:56.341 --> 27:58.426
So that's what he's been up to all along.

27:59.844 --> 28:00.804
While deceiving me.

28:02.764 --> 28:03.890
Yes, truthfully…

28:06.309 --> 28:08.186
what we did wasn't really lessons.

28:10.063 --> 28:13.483
Mr. Heo covets stories
and gets swept up in them quickly…

28:16.194 --> 28:18.530
but he doesn't know
which stories truly matter.

28:24.536 --> 28:27.414
What's more,
you don't exist in his stories.

28:30.500 --> 28:31.835
Yeah, I know.

28:34.546 --> 28:35.839
The truth is,

28:37.632 --> 28:39.676
I've known for a long time.

28:46.641 --> 28:47.851
But why are you…

28:50.145 --> 28:52.147
telling me all this?

28:59.904 --> 29:00.864
I'll tell you that…

29:04.200 --> 29:05.118
next time.

29:07.120 --> 29:09.247
We met a few more times after that

29:10.206 --> 29:11.916
and became friends.

29:13.042 --> 29:17.088
What the fuck is this bullshit?

29:21.050 --> 29:21.968
Did you sleep with him?

29:26.723 --> 29:28.224
Is that important right now?

29:28.808 --> 29:30.518
Is that all you care about?

29:32.395 --> 29:33.730
Kang was right.

29:34.230 --> 29:36.274
Even now, you don't know what to ask.

29:36.357 --> 29:38.443
You have no idea what's truly important.

29:39.652 --> 29:41.946
Then what's important right now? Tell me.

29:42.614 --> 29:43.656
No, I won't.

29:44.157 --> 29:46.618
Because we're nothing to each other now.

29:49.204 --> 29:50.455
What did you say?

29:51.331 --> 29:52.457
Don't you get it?

29:52.957 --> 29:54.876
I won't live with you anymore.

29:55.919 --> 29:58.129
I won't put up with you anymore.

30:00.840 --> 30:04.052
I'm going to start writing
my own story now.

30:14.938 --> 30:15.855
Jo Hyeon-suk.

30:19.818 --> 30:21.110
Jo Hyeon-suk.

30:24.405 --> 30:25.740
Hyeon-suk!

30:45.218 --> 30:46.761
Hyeon-suk, don't go.

30:49.389 --> 30:51.307
Please don't go, Jo Hyeon-suk.

30:53.935 --> 30:55.144
Don't go.

31:02.944 --> 31:04.070
What the heck…

31:06.030 --> 31:07.323
What is this?

31:10.910 --> 31:11.828
What…

31:21.296 --> 31:22.130
Yeah?

31:22.213 --> 31:25.133
Mun-oh, something terrible has happened!

31:25.216 --> 31:26.968
Have you seen the school forum?

31:27.468 --> 31:28.636
It's blowing up.

31:30.388 --> 31:31.723
What about the forum?

31:33.016 --> 31:33.975
Just tell me.

31:34.934 --> 31:38.146
Well, I don't know how to explain it…

31:40.148 --> 31:42.358
Come on, what are you trying to say?

31:43.359 --> 31:44.569
Just read it to me.

31:45.778 --> 31:48.698
Okay, then.
I'll just read you a few sentences.

31:49.616 --> 31:53.995
"Professor Heo Mun-oh forced me
to write defamatory content

31:54.078 --> 31:55.955
about the author Kim Su-hun."

31:57.373 --> 31:58.708
"Blinded by jealousy,

31:58.791 --> 32:02.378
he fabricated false information
with the intention

32:02.462 --> 32:04.881
of destroying Kim Su-hun's reputation."

32:06.007 --> 32:09.802
"Once I caught on to his intentions,
he tried to bribe me by offering

32:09.886 --> 32:14.432
to slip me the problems
of the programming competition in return."

32:14.515 --> 32:16.851
"When I refused to be coerced any longer,

32:17.435 --> 32:19.812
he even stole my work
and claimed it as his own…"

32:19.896 --> 32:23.274
Well, anyway, that's the gist of it.

32:23.358 --> 32:25.151
It was posted anonymously,

32:25.234 --> 32:28.655
and they even warned that they'd upload
that novel as evidence soon.

32:28.738 --> 32:29.906
The thing is,

32:30.406 --> 32:32.575
the view count keeps… It's skyrocketing.

32:33.868 --> 32:35.870
And people keep posting comments.

32:36.371 --> 32:37.246
Mun-oh.

32:37.914 --> 32:40.249
What's all this about?
It's not true, is it?

32:52.637 --> 32:53.471
My novel.

32:54.597 --> 32:56.015
Where's my novel?

32:56.557 --> 32:57.934
Where did my novel go?

33:00.770 --> 33:02.105
Where did my novel go?

33:03.398 --> 33:04.315
My novel.

33:05.274 --> 33:07.694
Where did my novel go? My novel.

33:10.321 --> 33:13.616
Lee Kang, you bastard. You took my novel?

33:14.117 --> 33:15.535
How dare you touch my novel.

33:16.035 --> 33:18.871
The number you have dialed
is not in service.

33:18.955 --> 33:21.207
-What?
-Please check and try again.

33:21.290 --> 33:22.834
You son of a bitch.

33:25.503 --> 33:28.381
The number you have dialed
is not in service.

33:28.464 --> 33:30.174
You son of a bitch!

33:30.258 --> 33:33.094
You motherfucker!
You little son of a bitch!

33:33.177 --> 33:35.513
You son of a bitch!

33:36.264 --> 33:37.348
You took my novel…

33:37.432 --> 33:40.935
You can't! You son of a bitch. No.

33:41.019 --> 33:42.770
You son of a bitch!

33:44.897 --> 33:45.773
Lee Kang.

33:46.816 --> 33:48.192
That son of a bitch!

33:49.444 --> 33:50.820
Why would you…

33:52.405 --> 33:54.198
Why did you do this to me?

33:54.699 --> 33:56.367
Why me?

33:56.868 --> 33:59.203
Last week,
we reported on shocking allegations

33:59.287 --> 34:03.082
about a professor
at a prestigious university in Seoul.

34:03.166 --> 34:06.044
-That's him, right?
-A post on the online forum claimed

34:06.127 --> 34:10.423
that he forced a student to write a novel
slandering renowned author Kim Su-hun.

34:11.215 --> 34:15.344
Today, the full novel was posted online
along with the professor's identity,

34:15.428 --> 34:17.555
causing an even bigger uproar.

34:18.056 --> 34:21.059
What's even more shocking about this novel

34:21.142 --> 34:25.396
is that it consistently depicts Kim Su-hun
as a bloodthirsty, psychopathic criminal.

34:27.899 --> 34:31.194
He can't even write his own work,
yet he slanders another writer.

34:50.338 --> 34:53.132
TRASH BELONGS IN THE TRASH CAN!

35:02.600 --> 35:05.812
In response,
Kim Su-hun's legal representative stated

35:05.895 --> 35:07.772
that they are preparing a lawsuit,

35:07.855 --> 35:10.358
as it amounts to deliberate
and serious defamation.

35:11.359 --> 35:13.027
Meanwhile, the school in question

35:13.111 --> 35:15.947
has decided to convene
the disciplinary committee.

35:16.030 --> 35:20.159
Public attention is focused on
how they will handle this situation.

35:37.677 --> 35:40.096
You were deceived by a student?

35:43.349 --> 35:45.685
You honestly expect us to believe that?

35:47.520 --> 35:50.022
Do you think
you can resolve this situation

35:50.106 --> 35:52.859
with this statement
full of pathetic excuses?

35:56.529 --> 36:00.992
How will you take responsibility
for our school's damaged reputation?

36:01.075 --> 36:03.119
It's humiliating.

36:03.202 --> 36:06.455
Our school is plastered all over
the news and YouTube every day…

36:09.208 --> 36:13.963
Your recent teaching record shows
you've been canceling a lot of classes

36:14.505 --> 36:16.048
and skipping faculty meetings.

36:16.924 --> 36:19.260
But the most serious issue here

36:19.760 --> 36:22.430
is you leaking the programming competition
test problems.

36:23.848 --> 36:25.433
This is outrageous.

36:26.309 --> 36:30.146
This isn't a matter of
whether you're fit to teach. It's a crime!

36:32.398 --> 36:33.441
Professor.

36:34.025 --> 36:35.651
Look here, Professor Heo Mun-oh.

36:38.863 --> 36:40.364
A confrontation? Please.

36:41.741 --> 36:44.285
Lee Kang is currently
on a leave of absence,

36:44.368 --> 36:46.913
and you said
you don't even have his number.

36:55.671 --> 36:56.505
Fine.

36:57.924 --> 37:03.054
Let's say you were indeed
completely deceived by Lee Kang.

37:04.222 --> 37:05.890
If that's true,

37:06.599 --> 37:07.767
why do you think

37:08.768 --> 37:10.478
that student did this?

37:29.038 --> 37:30.248
I don't know.

37:37.713 --> 37:39.632
I don't know why…

37:46.430 --> 37:48.182
he did this to me either.

39:03.841 --> 39:07.178
You bastard, stop calling me.
Wrong fucking number!

40:41.439 --> 40:43.524
It's been a while, Mr. Heo.

40:44.066 --> 40:44.942
This is Lee Kang.

40:46.318 --> 40:48.154
I sent you an email. Please check.

40:48.237 --> 40:49.989
You son of a bitch.

40:50.865 --> 40:53.576
That fucking bastard reached out?

41:14.013 --> 41:16.432
MR. HEO, HERE IS MY LAST ASSIGNMENT

41:17.683 --> 41:19.018
Mr. Heo.

41:19.852 --> 41:21.437
Have you been well?

41:22.396 --> 41:24.982
I hear you've been
desperately looking for me.

41:25.483 --> 41:28.444
I get it.
You must have a lot of questions.

41:29.153 --> 41:33.282
I'm writing this now
to repay you for your patience.

41:33.949 --> 41:37.453
I'd say…
this is my final writing assignment.

41:39.663 --> 41:41.415
Do you remember that day,

41:42.374 --> 41:44.210
twelve years ago?

41:46.045 --> 41:47.379
Twelve years ago?

42:05.022 --> 42:07.024
Are you going to keep sulking like that?

42:07.525 --> 42:08.609
We're almost there.

42:08.692 --> 42:10.486
You could've just gone by yourself.

42:11.612 --> 42:13.531
Why do you have to bother me like this?

42:14.114 --> 42:15.783
Bother you?

42:16.283 --> 42:19.119
I thought a change of scenery
might do you good.

42:20.287 --> 42:23.249
You've been frustrated lately,
since progress has been slow.

42:24.500 --> 42:29.171
If you get out and move around a little,
it might help with writer's block.

42:35.386 --> 42:37.388
Looks like we're almost at the orphanage.

42:37.471 --> 42:38.305
And

42:38.931 --> 42:40.766
what am I even supposed to do there?

42:40.849 --> 42:42.560
You don't have to do anything.

42:42.643 --> 42:45.646
Just go for a walk or read a book
while I'm working.

42:46.146 --> 42:48.148
Let's go eat
something delicious afterward.

42:56.282 --> 42:57.408
What is it?

42:58.450 --> 42:59.660
What's wrong?

43:10.170 --> 43:12.381
NEW DRIVER

43:17.720 --> 43:19.513
Honey, could you step outside?

43:34.737 --> 43:37.448
Why weren't you paying attention
to the road?

43:37.531 --> 43:38.824
What should we do?

43:41.285 --> 43:42.494
Did we get a flat?

43:48.292 --> 43:52.713
If one of your friends gives an answer
and you also have it,

43:53.213 --> 43:57.009
you can add a "me too" sticker.

43:57.092 --> 43:59.595
And when you complete a bingo line,

43:59.678 --> 44:01.639
you shout "Bingo!"

44:01.722 --> 44:04.475
Bingo!

44:04.558 --> 44:08.270
So, for example,
what's your favorite fruit?

44:08.354 --> 44:09.355
-Lame.
-Watermelon.

44:09.438 --> 44:10.773
Watermelon? Then…

44:12.107 --> 44:13.484
This is boring.

44:16.945 --> 44:17.780
Miss?

44:18.530 --> 44:19.365
Yes?

44:19.865 --> 44:21.909
Do I have to do this?

44:23.410 --> 44:25.496
I guess you don't have to.

44:26.455 --> 44:30.292
If you don't want to,
you can just watch the others.

44:31.168 --> 44:32.002
Okay?

45:24.471 --> 45:25.305
How old are you?

45:27.266 --> 45:29.893
Why do adults always ask
that sort of thing?

45:31.311 --> 45:32.813
How old are you, mister?

45:37.317 --> 45:39.903
Please tell me. How old are you?

45:41.905 --> 45:43.407
I'm eight.

45:47.119 --> 45:48.579
Earlier, why didn't you

45:49.955 --> 45:51.206
want to get counseling?

45:54.793 --> 45:56.211
Was it really too lame?

45:57.671 --> 46:00.466
They always ask me to talk about
my mom and dad anyway.

46:02.843 --> 46:04.052
It's annoying.

46:07.598 --> 46:10.434
Talk about your mom and dad? Like what?

46:10.517 --> 46:12.269
I said I won't talk about them.

46:15.022 --> 46:17.274
If I talk about them to just anyone,

46:17.775 --> 46:19.735
Mom and Dad would be sad.

46:27.284 --> 46:28.452
Is that so?

46:32.247 --> 46:33.373
Then,

46:34.124 --> 46:36.752
instead of talking about your mom and dad…

46:38.921 --> 46:41.715
Stand up. You can't see them
from down here.

46:43.634 --> 46:46.261
There. Do you see those ducks over there?

46:47.846 --> 46:49.223
How about

46:49.932 --> 46:51.600
we talk about those ducks?

46:52.726 --> 46:54.561
-Ducks?
-Yeah, ducks.

46:56.271 --> 46:57.231
Okay, watch.

46:57.314 --> 47:01.193
Do you see that tiny baby duck over there?

47:01.693 --> 47:02.736
You see it?

47:04.029 --> 47:05.364
That's you.

47:06.323 --> 47:09.952
And you see that bigger duck
in front of it?

47:10.452 --> 47:11.995
That bigger duck is your mom.

47:13.247 --> 47:16.458
And the duck next to her is your dad.

47:18.460 --> 47:19.503
And so,

47:20.420 --> 47:23.006
we try talking about the duck family.

47:24.258 --> 47:25.300
That

47:26.593 --> 47:28.178
is called a story.

47:29.930 --> 47:30.973
A story?

47:31.056 --> 47:31.932
Yeah, a story.

47:35.185 --> 47:36.103
Why

47:36.687 --> 47:38.313
was that baby duck

47:38.939 --> 47:41.900
so annoyed earlier?

47:44.653 --> 47:45.904
And

47:47.573 --> 47:49.741
why is he so angry now?

48:06.091 --> 48:07.801
Because he misses them.

48:11.763 --> 48:13.307
The mom duck.

48:17.227 --> 48:18.729
The dad duck.

48:22.399 --> 48:23.358
Every day.

48:26.570 --> 48:27.863
Because…

48:31.742 --> 48:34.703
he misses them every night.

48:37.789 --> 48:39.750
Thanks to him, the little boy

48:40.459 --> 48:42.085
learned what stories were.

48:42.586 --> 48:44.379
Thanks to the duck family story,

48:44.463 --> 48:46.798
he was able to open up
about his mom and dad

48:46.882 --> 48:49.259
after holding it in for so long.

48:53.764 --> 48:55.390
The dad duck

48:56.558 --> 48:58.268
was really strong.

48:58.769 --> 49:01.521
The little boy cherished that moment.

49:02.105 --> 49:05.233
He felt like he was truly opening up
without any defiance or resistance

49:05.317 --> 49:09.696
for the first time
since coming to the orphanage.

49:11.865 --> 49:13.116
And where did they go?

49:15.035 --> 49:18.121
The dad duck had a truck.

49:18.205 --> 49:20.540
When the baby duck laughed,

49:21.458 --> 49:23.460
the mom duck would laugh along.

49:24.920 --> 49:28.840
The baby duck was really happy.

49:31.510 --> 49:34.513
Thank you so much for coming all this way.

49:35.138 --> 49:36.556
Don't mention it.

49:36.640 --> 49:39.309
I needed to do it for my practicum anyway.

49:39.810 --> 49:44.147
I'm the one who should be thanking you
for reaching out to me first.

49:53.198 --> 49:55.033
I'll be going, then.

49:55.117 --> 49:56.535
Have a safe trip back.

49:56.618 --> 49:58.537
-Thank you.
-Thank you for coming.

50:02.791 --> 50:04.209
Miss?

50:05.377 --> 50:07.587
Oh, it's you.

50:08.213 --> 50:09.589
Where's the male teacher?

50:10.590 --> 50:13.010
Male teacher? Oh!

50:14.594 --> 50:17.723
Well, he should be around here somewhere.

50:19.975 --> 50:21.518
Why do you ask?

50:35.574 --> 50:37.242
What's gotten into you?

50:43.999 --> 50:45.876
Something peculiar happened just now.

50:46.376 --> 50:48.962
You know that boy
you were talking to earlier?

50:49.046 --> 50:51.298
I saw the two of you talking.

50:51.798 --> 50:53.550
He came up to me just now

50:54.051 --> 50:56.845
and asked me for your address,

50:56.928 --> 50:58.764
saying he wanted to write to you.

50:58.847 --> 51:01.767
I guess he really enjoyed talking to you.

51:01.850 --> 51:03.602
It made me proud.

51:03.685 --> 51:05.395
What did you two talk about?

51:05.937 --> 51:07.355
And did you give it to him?

51:07.856 --> 51:09.691
Of course I did. Isn't he adorable?

51:09.775 --> 51:11.526
His name is Lee Kang.

51:11.610 --> 51:14.780
Why did you give it to him? What a hassle!

51:15.280 --> 51:17.157
I thought you two had a fun chat.

51:17.240 --> 51:18.867
What do you mean "fun"?

51:18.950 --> 51:21.411
I was just hearing him out
because he was talking.

51:21.495 --> 51:24.289
I asked him to see
if I could get inspired,

51:25.040 --> 51:29.461
but his parents died
in a truck accident or something.

51:29.544 --> 51:32.547
Anyway, it's the same old sob story.
Nothing new.

51:34.716 --> 51:36.968
What do you mean "nothing new"?

51:37.469 --> 51:39.137
How can you call it a sob story?

51:39.638 --> 51:42.099
Of course the kids here
have been through a lot.

51:42.182 --> 51:43.975
Yeah, and so what?

51:44.476 --> 51:46.812
A story still has to be riveting.

51:46.895 --> 51:49.773
It needs a special something
to make it a story.

51:50.816 --> 51:53.026
Anyway, forget it. Let's go.

51:53.110 --> 51:55.904
If he writes to me,
I'll cut him off on my end.

51:56.404 --> 51:58.990
Hurry up. Hand me the keys. I'll drive.

52:18.468 --> 52:20.387
YEONSEO UNIVERSITY
PROFESSOR HEO MUN-OH

52:34.901 --> 52:36.862
WELCOME, FRESHMEN OF YEONSEO UNIVERSITY

52:52.627 --> 52:55.422
PROFESSOR'S OFFICE, HEO MUN-OH

52:56.047 --> 52:59.259
Where's the department office?
Maybe it's on a different floor?

52:59.885 --> 53:01.011
Let's go over there.

53:02.262 --> 53:03.638
Oh? Heo Mun-oh?

53:05.098 --> 53:08.101
I signed up for his class this semester.
Basic Composition.

53:08.185 --> 53:11.563
I heard you should steer clear of him.
That his classes are hard.

53:11.646 --> 53:14.649
Guess what? Professor Heo Mun-oh
went to college with my dad.

53:14.733 --> 53:15.817
Wanna know the kicker?

53:16.318 --> 53:19.154
He had the hugest crush on my mom
when they were students.

53:19.654 --> 53:22.908
And he used to get jealous of my dad
during composition class.

53:22.991 --> 53:25.452
I overheard my parents
talking about it once.

53:26.953 --> 53:29.122
He had a crush on your mom? Small world.

53:50.101 --> 53:53.438
Are you in YDOC too?
They gave these as freshmen goodies.

53:57.067 --> 54:00.278
I'm Kim Se-yun, class of '25.
Library and Information Science. You?

54:00.362 --> 54:02.530
Lee Kang, class of '25.
Electronics Engineering.

54:25.095 --> 54:28.682
Yun. Kids? Come and have some snacks.

54:37.190 --> 54:38.483
-Eat up, kids.
-Wow.

54:38.566 --> 54:40.277
-Thank you for the food!
-Thank you.

54:40.360 --> 54:41.403
-Looks good.
-Enjoy.

54:41.486 --> 54:42.487
The truth is,

54:44.030 --> 54:45.991
there never was a housekeeper.

54:47.200 --> 54:48.994
Our lessons are over.

54:49.494 --> 54:50.620
Over!

54:54.332 --> 54:55.417
What the…

54:55.500 --> 54:56.418
Oh my God!

54:58.378 --> 55:00.255
-Oh my God!
-Was there an accident?

55:04.884 --> 55:06.761
Oh no, she's bleeding. Hurry!

55:06.845 --> 55:09.139
That's when I remembered what you said.

55:11.558 --> 55:13.810
That for a story to be a story,

55:15.687 --> 55:18.231
it needs a special something.

55:20.400 --> 55:21.693
That's her.

55:25.155 --> 55:26.072
Min-hui.

55:28.033 --> 55:28.992
What did you say?

55:29.576 --> 55:30.410
That's Mr. Kim.

55:31.202 --> 55:32.871
Where?

55:46.217 --> 55:47.302
That man is…

55:49.095 --> 55:50.305
Mr. Kim?

55:51.931 --> 55:53.224
Se-yun's dad?

56:03.360 --> 56:04.486
The accident…

56:06.571 --> 56:08.406
was an unforeseen coincidence.

56:09.032 --> 56:09.949
Mr. Kim!

56:10.450 --> 56:11.910
-President Choi.
-Ma'am!

56:11.993 --> 56:13.578
-There.
-Right.

56:13.661 --> 56:16.164
-What do we do?
-She works for our publishing house!

56:16.831 --> 56:20.001
-Yes, I'll go with her.
-Oh, how awful!

56:41.147 --> 56:42.148
Welcome--

56:44.734 --> 56:45.610
Mr. Heo.

56:47.028 --> 56:50.532
And what's more,
that unfortunate incident happened.

56:51.032 --> 56:54.202
But for the sake of your studies,

56:54.786 --> 56:57.414
I think it'd only be my duty as a teacher…

56:57.497 --> 57:00.583
From that point on,
the writer of this story

57:01.084 --> 57:02.293
was always you.

57:05.880 --> 57:07.173
Kid.

57:07.966 --> 57:09.968
Why do you look so troubled these days?

57:10.635 --> 57:13.221
Is something worrying you?

57:16.266 --> 57:18.268
I just have something to do.

57:19.310 --> 57:20.770
But it's almost done.

57:21.771 --> 57:23.731
Is your part-time job wearing you down?

57:24.566 --> 57:25.942
If so, kid,

57:26.443 --> 57:28.570
don't feel like you have to visit.

57:29.571 --> 57:31.573
Why do you keep coming?

57:33.867 --> 57:36.286
If you don't want to see me,
get better already.

57:37.745 --> 57:38.997
Because to me, Director,

57:40.540 --> 57:42.375
you're both parents.

57:42.876 --> 57:44.210
My mom and dad.

57:44.294 --> 57:46.880
For goodness' sake, kiddo.

57:48.047 --> 57:52.010
I quit being the director
of the orphanage ages ago.

58:07.817 --> 58:08.735
And so…

58:10.653 --> 58:13.156
how is your story?

58:14.365 --> 58:15.408
You punk!

58:15.492 --> 58:17.869
You listen to me carefully.
This isn't fabrication.

58:17.952 --> 58:20.872
This is the truth.
An undeniable truth based on all we know.

58:33.259 --> 58:36.179
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW
BY HEO MUN-OH

58:41.059 --> 58:42.560
This is my novel.

58:44.938 --> 58:45.897
This is mine.

58:47.148 --> 58:48.650
My second novel.

58:57.408 --> 58:58.493
So…

59:00.787 --> 59:03.206
how is your story?

59:08.836 --> 59:10.380
Is your story

59:11.881 --> 59:13.174
special?

59:25.228 --> 59:26.312
Unreal.

59:28.815 --> 59:29.649
Unreal.

59:35.822 --> 59:36.948
Unreal.

01:00:24.662 --> 01:00:25.705
So that was it?

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:33.588
It was all because of that?

01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:40.928
That was it?

01:01:05.119 --> 01:01:07.705
Damn you!

01:01:07.789 --> 01:01:08.831
Son of a bitch.

01:01:38.403 --> 01:01:39.904
Has your story

01:01:40.405 --> 01:01:41.489
finally become

01:01:43.324 --> 01:01:44.909
special?

01:03:12.371 --> 01:03:13.664
Faust.

01:03:14.165 --> 01:03:17.293
So there are still folks
who read classics like this.

01:03:18.753 --> 01:03:21.923
It's even more of a fun read
if you know how it was written.

01:03:23.257 --> 01:03:24.425
That'll be 13,000 won.

01:03:27.929 --> 01:03:29.180
I already know.

01:03:32.266 --> 01:03:34.185
For over 60 years,

01:03:35.311 --> 01:03:37.438
it was constantly added to and revised.

01:04:23.568 --> 01:04:24.652
I'd like to resume

01:04:25.945 --> 01:04:27.196
our literature lessons.

01:04:33.327 --> 01:04:35.663
I now have a story I really want to write.

01:05:07.653 --> 01:05:08.738
What story?

01:05:23.461 --> 01:05:25.546
To be continued..

01:05:26.047 --> 01:05:29.050
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

01:07:55.112 --> 01:08:00.117
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
